From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:45:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Support range input values, UA style and thumb colours

Range inputs previously got no special data, so paint had no value to
display. Seed RangeInput(value) at layout construction from the
value/min/max attributes (HTML default: range midpoint) and keep an
existing variant across construct passes so a live IDL value set by the
embedder survives. range_input_value() is the accessor for the paint
layer.

str::parse::<f64>() accepts "NaN", "inf" and "-inf", and f64::clamp
panics on NaN or min > max, so <input type=range min=NaN> would take the
whole layout down. Parses go through is_finite() before clamping.

The generic input border/padding/background painted a box around the
slider widget. Chrome's UA sheet strips these for range; width mirrors
Chrome's 129px default intrinsic size.

The servo stylo build drops rules with unknown vendor pseudo-elements,
but pre-accent-color pages (Bootstrap's .form-range included) theme
sliders exclusively via ::-webkit-slider-thumb / ::-moz-range-thumb
background colors. Rewrite at parse time: append a synthesized
'<selector-sans-pseudo> { accent-color: <color> }' rule for every thumb
rule carrying a background color, at all three parse sites (<style>,
linked sheets, @import). Selector matching and specificity then work
naturally; the UA slider paint reads the computed accent-color.
Appending only; a mis-parse can skip a rewrite but never corrupt the
sheet.
